  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nAn upper-level trough associated with a surface cold front is \nexiting North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana this \nafternoon. This will bring cool (below seasonal average) \ntemperatures to the area with lingering rain showers.  On Saturday \nan upper-level ridge builds in briefly over North-central, Central, \nand Southwestern Montana. This will bring mostly dry weather with \nstatus quo temperatures to the area. On Saturday along the Rocky \nMountain Front there will be snow mixed with rain at times and \nprimarily all rain at lower elevations. On Sunday a closed upper-\nlevel low will move over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana with a 700mb low moving over southern Alberta/the Hi-Line. \nThis will bring strong southerly flow aloft which will bring \nstrong winds to north-south orientated valleys of Southwestern \nMontana. On Sunday along the higher peaks of the Rocky Mountain \nFront there will be snow with the rest of the Rocky Mountain Front\nseeing rain and/or a rain/snow mix. On Sunday across the rest of \nNorth-central Montana there will be light rain showers. On Sunday \nwarm air advection will bring seasonable temperatures to \nSouthwestern Montana with below seasonal average temperatures \nnorth of the I-90 corridor. \n\nOn Monday the upper-level low exits North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. Precipitation will linger across North-central \nMontana on Monday. On Monday low-level winds will increase which \nwill bring at least breezy conditions to North-central Montana. On\nMonday temperatures will remain cool. Tuesday through Thursday an\nupper-level ridge gradually builds in over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will allow temperatures to\nwarm back up to near seasonal averages with mostly dry weather. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Sunday there is a 40 - 80% chance for sustained winds of 40 mph \nand a 50% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or greater in the Madison \nRiver Valley. As a result a High Wind Watch was issued for the \nMadison River Valley from 12 PM to 9 PM on Sunday. On Sunday \nthere is greater than a 50% chance for 55 mph wind gusts along the\nridgetops of the Madison and Gallatin Mountains. On Monday there \nis a 30 - 50% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or greater across \nmost of North-central Montana. \n\nOn Sunday there are differences in the 700 mb low track between the \nGFS and Euro. The Euro the low tracking slightly further south \nwhich would bring more precipitation/snow to the Northern Rocky \nMountain Front than what the GFS has. There is a 50 - 80% chance \nfor one inch of snow or greater along the majority of the Rocky \nMountain Front Sunday into Monday. There is a low chance that \nisolated mountain peaks will receive in excess of 6 inches of \nsnowfall Sunday into Monday. On Tuesday morning there is a 40 - \n60% chance for low temperatures of 36 degrees or colder across the\nHi-Line and the valleys of Southwestern Montana. -IG",
